    id: "homa-bay-cities-v2",
    type: "city",
    parent: "KE-43",
    coords: [34.4531, -0.5273],
    name: {
      de: "Homa Bay",
      hu: "Homa Bay",
      ro: "Homa Bay",
      en: "Homa Bay"},
    image: "/poi-images/homa-bay-cities-v2.webp",
    descriptionAdvanced: {
      de: "Homa Bay liegt am malerischen südlichen Ufer des Viktoriasees und ist die Verwaltungshauptstadt des Homa Bay Countys. Die Wirtschaft der Stadt ist stark von der Fischerei geprägt, insbesondere dem Fang von Nilbarsch und Tilapia, sowie der Landwirtschaft auf dem fruchtbaren Boden der Umgebung. Homa Bay ist der ideale Ausgangspunkt für Besuche im Ruma-Nationalpark, dem einzigen Ort in Kenia, an dem die seltene Pferdeantilope (Roan Antelope) in freier Wildbahn beobachtet werden kann. Die Stadt wird im Hintergrund von den Homa-Bergen (Mount Homa) überragt, einer Reihe erloschener vulkanischer Hügel. Homa Bay spielt eine zentrale Rolle in der Luo-Kultur und ist ein wichtiges Zentrum für den Binnenhandel auf dem Viktoriasee (Biologie & Geografie K7).",
      hu: "Homa Bay egy pezsgő partmenti város a Viktória-tó keleti öblében, a tókörnyéki halászat egyik fellegvára. A város a Homa-hegy, egy régi vulkáni hegy lábánál épült. A gazdaság jelentős része a tilápia és a nílusi sügér halászatán alapul, amelyeket belföldre és exportra is szánnak. A közeli Ruma Nemzeti Park miatt a régió egyre vonzóbb a turisták számára, a helyi luo közösség pedig gazdag folklórral és mesterségekkel várja a látogatókat. (Természetismeret K5 — halászat és tóvidékek)",
      ro: "Homa Bay este un oraș pitoresc situat pe malul estic al Golfului Winam, în extremitatea estică a Lacului Victoria. Datorită poziției sale, economia orașului este profund ancorată în industria pescuitului, capturile de biban de Nil și tilapia susținând o mare parte din populația locală a comunității Luo. Orașul servește drept punct de plecare excelent pentru explorarea atracțiilor naturale uimitoare din regiune, cum ar fi Muntele Homa, situl paleontologic de la Kanam și Parcul Național Ruma, singurul loc din Kenya unde poate fi admirată rara antilopă roană.",
      en: "Homa Bay is a prominent port town situated on the southern shores of the Winam Gulf of Lake Victoria, framed by the backdrop of the volcanic Mount Homa. Established in the mid-20th century, the town has grown primarily as a fishing and agricultural center, heavily reliant on the lake's resources, particularly the Nile perch and tilapia fisheries. The surrounding topography is distinguished by the nearby Ruma National Park, gazetted in 1983, which protects one of the last remaining populations of the endangered roan antelope in Kenya. The local climate is warm and semi-humid, supporting the cultivation of sorghum, maize, and cotton in the hinterlands. Recent infrastructural investments have sought to revive passenger and cargo ferry services across the lake to Kisumu and neighboring countries. Economics K6 — Lake economies and fishing."
    },
    factsAdvanced: {
      en: ["Located on the southern shores of Lake Victoria's Winam Gulf.", "Serves as the administrative headquarters of Homa Bay County.", "Mount Homa, a broad volcanic complex, is located 20 kilometers north.", "Ruma National Park, known for roan antelopes, was gazetted in 1983.", "The local economy relies heavily on the Nile perch and tilapia fishing industries.", "Situated at an elevation of approximately 1,135 meters (3,724 feet).", "The town's population was recorded at roughly 112,000 in the 2019 census."]
    },
    
